# Cursor: read AGENTS.md first

AGENTS.md is the single owner of the working rules for this repo. Read it at the start of every
session, before writing anything.

Short version:

1. Run `make sync` before you start. It pulls the team's work and loads their shared memory.
2. Read `memory/SHARED.md`, then `docs/brief.md`, `docs/01-idea.md`, `docs/02-system.md`,
   `docs/decisions.md`.
3. Work only in the paths your workstream owns: `OWNERS.md`.
4. Every number the note quotes comes from `results/`. Regenerate, never hand-edit.
5. Write the hypothesis and the falsifier before looking at results. Never open the
   out-of-sample window except on the run that reports it.
6. Never commit credentials, absolute local paths, or anything under `data/`.

Capture is mechanical: `.githooks/pre-commit` refreshes the shared memory on every commit, and
`hippo hook install cursor` wires the Cursor wrapper on your machine. See `docs/memory.md`.

<!-- hippo:start -->
# Project Memory (Hippo)
# Before each task, load context:
#   hippo context --auto --budget 1500
# After errors:
#   hippo remember "<error description>" --error
# After completing:
#   hippo outcome --good
<!-- hippo:end -->
